#!/bin/sh
# Dodona enforcement layer 2: git itself refuses a commit made from the SHARED CHECKOUT.
#
# Source of truth for this file is .claude/hooks/pre-commit (tracked). tools/dev.ps1 copies
# it into the repository's .git/hooks/ on every run, because .git/hooks is not versioned and
# an install step someone has to remember is not enforcement (CLAUDE.md 0.3 / D-6). That is
# the same reason DeployGate writes .git/info/exclude rather than asking.
#
# WHY A SECOND LAYER. Layer 1 (.claude/hooks/no-main-tree.ps1) is a PreToolUse hook, so it
# binds the Edit/Write tools and nothing else: a heredoc, sed, or a shell redirect writes
# into the shared checkout without ever consulting it. Git runs THIS with no agent
# cooperation at all, at the boundary where the damage actually became permanent -- f9aaf25
# was a COMMIT that carried another lane's work, not an edit. Gate plus backstop, the same
# pair as the claim gate and the merge-time diff (design 6).
#
# THE TEST, same stateless one as layer 1: git leaves `.git` as a FILE in a worktree and a
# DIRECTORY in the main checkout. No registry, no lock, nothing that can go stale or jam.
#
# SCOPED TO THIS REPOSITORY ON PURPOSE. Never `git config --global core.hooksPath`: all 11
# suites build temp repos and run `git commit -m init` in them, every one of those a main
# checkout, and a global install would abort all of them. Checked before installing.

# The one deliberate override (D-7 item 4), same variable as layer 1: sometimes the shared
# checkout is genuinely right -- a release commit, or installing these hooks. A choice you
# make, never a wall you hit (CLAUDE.md 0.1).
if [ "$DODONA_ALLOW_MAIN_TREE" = "1" ]; then
    exit 0
fi

top=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel 2>/dev/null) || exit 0
[ -n "$top" ] || exit 0

# A FILE means worktree, which is where work belongs. Only a DIRECTORY is the shared checkout.
if [ ! -d "$top/.git" ]; then
    exit 0
fi

name="w$(date +%m%d-%H%M)"
cat >&2 <<MSG

COMMIT REFUSED -- this is the shared checkout ($top), not a worktree.

Two sessions in one checkout cannot tell whose edit is whose, and this is the boundary
where that becomes permanent: f9aaf25 committed another lane's lanes.cwd migration and
Ver.cs changes along with its own routing fix, because both sat in the same working tree.

Move the work to a tree of its own:
    powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools/dev.ps1 worktree $name
    git -C .claude/worktrees/$name ...      # commit from there

If the shared checkout is genuinely the right place (a release commit, installing hooks):
    DODONA_ALLOW_MAIN_TREE=1 git commit ...

This is Dodona enforcement layer 2 (RECOVERY-PHASES D-7). Layer 1 is the PreToolUse hook
in .claude/settings.json; this one exists because layer 1 cannot see a shell redirect.
MSG
exit 1
